            <ArticleTitle>Reversible covalent interactions of β-aminoboronic acids with carbohydrate derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1809-1812</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09640a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>β-Aminoalkylboronic acids are capable of binding to carbohydrate derivatives through reversible covalent interactions. An anthracene-bearing β-aminoboronic acid has been synthesized, enabling determinations of association constants for binding of sugars by fluorescence spectroscopy. The diol-binding properties of β-aminoboronic acids are also useful in catalysis: one such compound displays remarkably high activity for regioselective O-acylation of a pyranoside derivative.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
